---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Balance Chemical Equation"
  description="Read our Privacy Policy. Learn how Balance Chemical Equation protects your privacy with 100% client-side reaction computing and transparent data practices."
  currentPath="/privacy-policy"
  lang="en"
>
  <div class="relative py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-20 border-b border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626] overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Mesh Glow -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 hero-mesh-gradient pointer-events-none opacity-60"></div>

    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#737373] mb-4 sm:mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#171717] dark:hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] font-medium">Privacy Policy</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-white dark:bg-[#171717] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#333333] text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-mono font-medium mb-4 shadow-[0px_1px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)]">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 shrink-0"></span>
        <span>EFFECTIVE DATE: NOVEMBER 2026</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-[28px] sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:tracking-[-1.5px] text-[#171717] dark:text-white leading-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 sm:mt-4 text-sm sm:text-lg text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1] leading-relaxed">
        At <strong>balancechemicalequation.com</strong>, we are deeply committed to protecting your personal privacy. Our chemistry computation tools are engineered from the ground up to respect user autonomy and minimize data collection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16 space-y-8 sm:space-y-12 text-[14px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
    <!-- Key Guarantee Banner -->
    <div class="p-4 sm:p-6 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/5 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] space-y-2">
      <div class="font-semibold text-sm sm:text-base text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>🔒</span> Core Privacy Guarantee: 100% Client-Side Engine
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
        All chemical equations, reaction inputs, stoichiometry conversions, molar mass calculations, and limiting reagent simulations you enter are executed strictly within your local web browser. Your formulas and scientific work are never uploaded to our servers, logged in databases, or sold to third parties.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Introduction -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        1. Introduction and Scope
      </h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy outlines how Balance Chemical Equation ("we", "us", or "our"), operating the website <strong class="text-[#171717] dark:text-white">balancechemicalequation.com</strong>, handles information when you visit or interact with our web services. By using our site, you acknowledge the terms outlined in this policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Information We Collect -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        2. Information We Collect and Receive
      </h2>
      <p>
        We practice data minimization and do not require user accounts, logins, or payment details to access our free equation balancer. Information collected falls into the following limited categories:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Technical & Infrastructure Logs:</strong> Like virtually all websites, our hosting servers may automatically record standard web server request logs, including your internet protocol (IP) address, browser user-agent, operating system, referring URL, and timestamp. These logs are used strictly for system security, denial-of-service mitigation, and infrastructure diagnostics.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Local Storage (Theme Preferences):</strong> We utilize your browser’s standard HTML5 <code class="font-mono text-xs px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-[#f2f2f2] dark:bg-[#1f1f1f] text-[#0070f3]">localStorage</code> to store your preferred interface theme (<code class="font-mono text-xs">light</code> or <code class="font-mono text-xs">dark</code>). This data resides exclusively on your local device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Direct Correspondence:</strong> If you contact us via email or our contact form, we collect the details you provide (such as your name, email address, and message contents) solely to respond to your inquiry.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Cookies and Advertising -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        3. Cookies and Third-Party Advertising
      </h2>
      <p>
        We may use standard HTTP cookies or partner with third-party advertising networks (such as Google AdSense) and privacy-focused analytics providers to maintain free access to our educational tools.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
        <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to our sites and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
        <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Data Protection Rights (GDPR & CCPA) -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        4. Your Rights Under GDPR & CCPA
      </h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your geographical location, you possess specific statutory rights regarding personal data:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-[#121212] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626]">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#171717] dark:text-white mb-1">European Union (GDPR)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#737373] leading-relaxed">
            You hold the right to access, rectify, request erasure, restrict processing, and request portability of any personal data retained under legal grounds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-[#121212] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626]">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#171717] dark:text-white mb-1">California Consumers (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#737373] leading-relaxed">
            We do not sell or share personal information. California residents have the right to request disclosure of information categories and request deletion without discrimination.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Children's Privacy -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        5. Children's Privacy (COPPA)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Our chemistry tools are designed for general academic and educational use. We do not knowingly collect personal identifiable information from children under 13. If you believe a child has submitted personal details through our contact forms, please contact us immediately for prompt deletion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. Policy Revisions -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        6. Updates to This Policy
      </h2>
      <p>
        We may occasionally update this Privacy Policy to reflect technical enhancements or statutory obligations. Any revisions will be reflected with an updated effective date at the top of this document. Continued use of the website following published updates signifies acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. Contact Us -->
    <section class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626]">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        7. Contacting Our Data Privacy Team
      </h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our privacy practices, please contact us at:
      </p>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[#171717] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#2e2e2e] font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1">
        <div>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@balancechemicalequation.com" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline break-all">privacy@balancechemicalequation.com</a></div>
        <div>Website: <a href="https://balancechemicalequation.com" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline break-all">https://balancechemicalequation.com</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

